%% request: how DNS resolution works
%% fixed from tool errors
flowchart TD
    User([👤 User types example.com]) --> Browser[Browser cache?]
    Browser -- hit --> Done([✅ Connect to IP])
    Browser -- miss --> OS[OS resolver cache?]
    OS -- hit --> Done
    OS -- miss --> Stub[Stub resolver /etc/resolv.conf]
    Stub --> Recursive[(Recursive resolver ISP or 8.8.8.8)]
    Recursive --> Cache{Cached and fresh?}
    Cache -- yes --> Answer[Return cached answer]
    Answer --> Done
    Cache -- no --> Root[[Root server .]]
    Root -- "referral to .com" --> TLD[[TLD server .com]]
    TLD -- "referral to ns1.example.com" --> Auth[[Authoritative server]]
    Auth -- "A record: 93.184.216.34 TTL 3600" --> Store[(Store in cache for TTL)]
    Store --> Answer

    Auth -. NXDOMAIN .-> Fail([❌ Name does not exist])
    Recursive -. timeout .-> Retry{Retry other NS?}
    Retry -- yes --> Auth
    Retry -- no --> Fail

    classDef cache fill:#fff7d1,stroke:#b38f00
    classDef server fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0
    class Browser,OS,Recursive,Store cache
    class Root,TLD,Auth server
